\nSo I am not necessarily complete \u2014 I may be waiting for a specific shape.\n\nBut with three melds and five in hand, I need to form a fourth meld and a pair from those five.\n\nPossible combinations:\n\nFrom hand: W6, W7, W7, T1, B9\n\nCan I form a chow or pung?\n\n- W6 and W7 \u2192 could go toward [W6,W7,W8] or [W5,W6,W7]\n- But W8? Unseen: 3 W8s, none used yet? Possible.\n- W5: unshown 3, so possible.\n\nBut I have no W5 or W8.\n\nT1: alone, terminal.\n\nB9: alone, terminal.\n\nBest pair: W7\u00d72\n\nSo likely, I will keep W7 pair, and try to form a fourth meld involving W6, T1, B9.\n\nBut hard.\n\nAlternative: perhaps I can form a chow with W6-W7-W8 or W5-W6-W7.\n\nBut missing third tile.\n\nOr, consider discarding a singleton to improve chances.\n\nNow evaluate valid actions:\n\n1. **Play W7**: discard one W7. Leaves W7 single. Breaks pair. Very bad \u2014 I have no other pair candidates. Unless I'm waiting for W6 or something, but unlikely. Avoid breaking pair.\n\n2. **Play W6**: discard W6. Then hand becomes W7\u00d72, T1, B9 \u2192 pair of W7, and two terminals. Still need to form fourth meld from T1 and B9 \u2014 impossible. But at least I keep a pair. W6 is somewhat safe \u2014 used in opponent's meld [W6,W7,W8], so possibly one already used, and I have one. Two used? My W6 and their W6 \u2192 two. Original 3 \u2192 one left. Risky to discard if someone needs it, but less likely.\n\n3. **Play T1**: discard T1. Hand: W6, W7\u00d72, B9. Pair W7. T1 is terminal, and early discard, but I\u2019ve held it a while. Previous player discarded T5, T6 \u2014 not indicative. T1 might be dangerous, but not clearly.\n\n4. **Play B9**: terminal, same issue.\n\nNow, scoring:\n\nIf I win with current structure, possible patterns:\n\n- **Outside Hand** (8 points): every meld contains terminal or honor. Check:\n  - [B6,B6,B6]: B6 is simple (6), not terminal \u2192 fails\n  - So not Outside Hand\n\n- **All Chows** (2 points): I have two chows and one pung \u2192 not el